<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Relationships slip when life gets busy: a follow-up you meant to send, how you met someone, whose
    birthday is next week. Philotes is a quiet place to keep that context for friends, family and
    colleagues. It runs on your own machine, with your data in your own database and nowhere else.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Remember the context</h3>
        <p>People, how you met, notes, labels, contact details, and how they are connected to each other.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Stay in touch</h3>
        <p>Log each conversation, set how often you want to reach someone, and see who is overdue and which dates are coming up.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Yours to run</h3>
        <p>One container beside Postgres. Import from Google Contacts, export whenever you like, and script it through the GraphQL API.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <pre class="code"><code>git clone https://github.com/cubicecho/philotes &amp;&amp; cd philotes
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32) docker compose up -d</code></pre>
    <p>Then open <a href="http://localhost:3000">http://localhost:3000</a>. Migrations run on startup.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    Full documentation lives in the project README:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}#readme" rel="noopener">{{ site.repo }}</a>
  </p>
